{
  "requirement": "Habeas MUST define its authoring configuration using these data structures:\n\n```text\nUserAuthoringConfig {\n    default: Optional<ConfigName>,\n    configs: Map<ConfigName, AuthoringConfig>,\n    projects: Map<CanonicalProjectRoot, ProjectSelection>,\n}\n\nWorkspaceAuthoringConfig {\n    default: Optional<ConfigName>,\n    configs: Map<ConfigName, AuthoringConfig>,  // omitted means empty\n}\n\nProjectSelection {\n    config: ConfigName,\n}\n\nAuthoringConfig {\n    backend: BackendConfig,                   // tagged union, flattened in TOML\n    concurrency: Optional<PositiveInteger>,   // simultaneous assessments\n    policy: Optional<AssessmentPolicy>,       // default: Confirm\n}\n\nAssessmentPolicy = Confirm | Once             // TOML: \"confirm\" or \"once\"\n\nBackendConfig = Bedrock(BedrockConfig) | Ollama(OllamaConfig)\n\nBedrockConfig {\n    model: ModelId,                           // model ID or inference-profile ID/ARN\n    aws_profile: Optional<String>,\n    region: Optional<String>,\n    credentials: Optional<BedrockCredentials>,\n    options: Map<String, OptionValue>,\n}\n\nBedrockCredentials {\n    access_key_id: SecretString,\n    secret_access_key: SecretString,\n    session_token: Optional<SecretString>,\n}\n\nOllamaConfig {\n    model: ModelId,                           // exact identifier, including tag\n    endpoint: Optional<String>,               // default: http://localhost:11434\n    api_key_env: Optional<EnvironmentVariableName>,\n    api_key: Optional<SecretString>,\n    options: Map<String, OptionValue>,\n}\n\nOptionValue = String | Boolean | Integer | FiniteFloat\n            | Array<OptionValue> | Map<String, OptionValue>\n\nSecretString = String                         // serialized normally; redacted in Debug\n\nModelRef {\n    backend: BackendKind,                     // Bedrock or Ollama\n    model: ModelId,\n}\n```\n\n`ModelRef` MUST be derived from the selected backend configuration and MUST\npreserve the exact model identifier. It MUST identify the model without replacing\nconnection settings such as AWS profile, region, or Ollama endpoint.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "The `AuthoringConfig` structure the requirement mandates is not fully defined in the code. The requirement says `AuthoringConfig` has `policy: Optional<AssessmentPolicy>` (default Confirm), and it defines `AssessmentPolicy = Confirm | Once` with TOML values \"confirm\" or \"once\".\n\n**What matches the requirement**\n- `src/config.rs` defines `WorkspaceAuthoringConfig` (`configs` defaults to empty), `UserAuthoringConfig` (`configs` required, `projects` optional), `ProjectSelection`, `BackendConfig` (a tagged union, flattened in `AuthoringConfig`), `BedrockConfig`, `BedrockCredentials`, `OllamaConfig`, `OptionValue`, `BackendKind` and `ModelRef`.\n- `SecretString` is a transparent string with a redacted `Debug` implementation (`src/config.rs` lines 85–104).\n- `BackendConfig::model_ref` (lines 415–428) builds `ModelRef` from the selected backend and copies the exact model string. It does not touch the profile, region or endpoint.\n- `OptionValue::validate` rejects non-finite floats.\n- Tests in `tests/configuration.rs` cover these items:\n  - round trips (`backend_configuration_round_trips_without_materializing_defaults`, `user_and_workspace_authoring_tables_round_trip_every_map`)\n  - `ModelRef` preserving the exact ARN and model ID alongside profile and region\n  - redaction of secrets in `Debug` output\n  - omitted workspace `configs` meaning empty\n\n**The gap**\n- `struct[AuthoringConfig]` (`src/config.rs` lines 139–148) has only `concurrency` and the flattened `backend`. There is no `policy` field.\n- A search of the repository for `AssessmentPolicy`, `policy: Option` and `Once` found no `AssessmentPolicy` type, no Confirm/Once enum, and no \"confirm\"/\"once\" TOML mapping. The only `policy` matches are unrelated path-access policy code.\n- The code does not define the `policy: Optional<AssessmentPolicy>` field or the `AssessmentPolicy` type, so the \"MUST define its authoring configuration using these data structures\" obligation is not met.\n- No `{fixme}` acknowledges this gap, and no test covers a `policy` field.\n\nBecause of this unacknowledged gap, the requirement is not satisfied.",
  "references": "e4fabd07890a5fbaeb527190d2251c8d664f89d3aef4d1899952d2f25c1c2d3f",
  "inputs": [
